hello this is presh talwalkar  this is the fourth video in the series  on how to solve the rubik's cube where i  explain how to solve the middle layer  we've solved the first layer  which means we have all of the edge  pieces matching the center  and all of the corner pieces in the  correct position with the correct  orientation  since the white layer is completely  solved what we're going to do is turn  the cube upside down  this will make it easier for us to see  the pieces that we want to identify to  solve the middle layer  the middle layer consists of four pieces  with two colors each  so let's see if any of these edge pieces  are on the top  so here we identify one of the pieces  which is red and green and we'll rotate  the red side so it matches the red side  here we have an orange and blue face  we'll deal with that in a moment  so now we have red matching the red side  and we want to move this to the right  so we're looking at the red side we're  matching the red side and we need to  move this edge piece to the right  so here's how we can do that without  messing anything else up  we go u  r  u prime  r prime  u prime  f prime  u  and finally f  and lo and behold we've moved the edge  piece to the middle  layer  in the correct orientation  and we haven't messed anything else up  so we'll continue solving the middle  layer we'll look for any of the edge  pieces that are on the top and here we  identify red and blue  so we're going to rotate this until the  red matches  the red center  and now  we need to move this piece to the left  so this is pretty much the same move as  when we moved it to the right but it'll  be  relative to the left  so we go u prime  l prime  u  l  u  f  u prime  and f prime  and now we put this red and blue piece  in the correct position  and every other piece that we've solved  so far in the bottom layer and the  middle layer has stayed in position  so now we're going to keep looking for  edge pieces  so here we have an orange and green  piece  and we're going to want to move we match  the orange to the center and we want to  move this to the left  so we do our same sequence of moves for  that we go  u prime  l prime  u  l  u  f  u prime  and f prime  we have one final piece  this is orange and blue and we need to  move it to the right so we're going to  use the move which moves it to the right  that's u  r  u prime  r prime  u prime  f prime  u  and f  and now we've solved the entire middle  layer  but before i go on to the next video i'm  just going  to show you one last thing  in this case we had all of the edge  pieces that were on the top and we  simply move them to where they need it  to be  but it might happen while you're solving  a cube  that you end up in an unlucky situation  so here's an example  where while we're looking around  you know we have this red and green  piece that's stuck  and sometimes you may you may need to  get that piece unstuck  so  if it's not on the top it's just stuck  in the middle layer  you need to get that to the top layer  so in order to do that what you can do  is you can use you can  you know move one of the other pieces  there so here we have an edge piece  that's on the top and we want to move it  to the right  so we use our move  which gets that piece  to the right side  and what that'll do is that'll un you  know that'll take out the edge piece  that was in the wrong spot and bump it  up to the top layer  so once we do that that red and green  piece we've moved it to the top  and now we can go ahead and solve the  rest of the cube  using the moves of left and right to get  to the middle layer  i'll go ahead and do that and now we  have to move this to the left so  i'll take care of  that and  using those two moves of left and right  we can always solve the middle layer  i hope you like this video please click  through to find out how to solve the  third and final layer  please subscribe to my channel  you can support me on patreon  catch me on my blo